  "reviews": [
    {
      "game": "V Rising",
      "game_image": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/products/11030/450x258/v-rising-pc-steam-cover.jpg?v=1791547200",
      "game_url": "https://www.instant-gaming.com/en/11030-buy-v-rising-pc-steam/",
      "user": "gamer-99cfc7",
      "avatar": "https://gaming-cdn.com/themes/igv2/images/avatar2.svg",
      "sentiment": "like",
      "content": "The game is awesome you got survival crafting and bosses to fight the only downside is the sun but your a vampire it's in the job description so to say , just be careful when the sun is up stai în the shadows and you'll live"
    },
    {
      "game": "Silent Hill: Townfall",
      "game_image": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/products/13086/450x258/silent-hill-townfall-pc-steam-cover.jpg?v=1791547200",
      "game_url": "https://www.instant-gaming.com/en/13086-buy-silent-hill-townfall-pc-steam/",
      "user": "gamer-4b88a73",
      "avatar": "https://gaming-cdn.com/themes/igv2/images/avatar2.svg",
      "sentiment": "like",
      "content": "I mean ....yaaaa?\n\n\n\nThe atmosphere, sound design and CRTV mechanic are really good, and some of the monsters are genuinely creepy. But the game feels way too slow for me. Most objectives force you to search for items, solve puzzles and backtrack instead of letting you explore naturally.\n\n\n\nThe Weight is also a cool concept, but its AI sometimes feels like it knows exactly where you are, which can make it frustrating instead of scary. I wish there was more action involved......almost stopped like 3 times\n\n\n\nGood game, but I wouldn't pay €50 for it, roughly €15–20."
    },
    {
      "game": "Ori and the Will of the Wisps",
      "game_image": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/products/19582/450x258/ori-and-the-will-of-the-wisps-pc-game-steam-cover.jpg?v=1791547200",
      "game_url": "https://www.instant-gaming.com/en/19582-buy-ori-and-the-will-of-the-wisps-pc-game-steam/",
      "user": "Arafel",
      "avatar": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/avatars/24143697-1791444694.jpg",
      "sentiment": "like",
      "content": "Ori and the Will of the Wisps is an absolutely beautiful game. Everything about it feels carefully crafted, from the stunning environments and fluid animations to the incredible soundtrack that makes every important moment feel even more emotional. The exploration is satisfying, the movement feels fantastic, and the platforming manages to be challenging without becoming frustrating. What surprised me most was how emotionally invested I became in the characters and their story. It has a wonderful way of combining atmosphere, gameplay, and music into something that feels genuinely memorable. It is one of those games where finishing it leaves you wishing you could experience it again for the first time. Truly an incredible experience and easily one of my favorite Metroidvania games."
    },
    {
      "game": "Hollow Knight",
      "game_image": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/products/2198/450x258/hollow-knight-pc-mac-steam-cover.jpg?v=1791547200",
      "game_url": "https://www.instant-gaming.com/en/2198-buy-hollow-knight-pc-mac-steam/",
      "user": "Arafel",
      "avatar": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/avatars/24143697-1791444694.jpg",
      "sentiment": "like",
      "content": "Hollow Knight is one of those games that manages to feel both beautiful and brutally unforgiving. The world of Hallownest is incredibly atmospheric, with a huge amount of exploration, secrets and lore that made me want to keep discovering what was around the next corner. The combat is simple to understand but difficult to master, and some bosses pushed my patience much further than I expected. I finished the story, but I still have 11 achievements left, which says a lot about just how much content there is beyond the main path. Not everything was equally enjoyable for me, especially some of the more demanding challenges, but the combination of exploration, atmosphere, music and satisfying combat makes Hollow Knight an unforgettable experience."
    }
  ],
